        {
          "name": "pqs:context",
          "value": "BIP32/secp256k1 converts the device master seed into the Monero wallet seed (which is then Keccak-reduced into edwards25519 spend/view scalars at monero_init.c:95-106). Shor breaks the secp256k1 HD layer as well as the ed25519 keys derived from it. The Monero protocol pins the downstream curves (replaceable only by a protocol fork), but the BIP32 layer is Ledger's own design and is changeable here."
        },
